=== regression mode note: individual-suite runs (both lanes). tests/run-all.sh is NOT usable as this task's regression evidence and is deliberately excluded: it runs a fixed ordered list of 60 suites under `set -euo pipefail` (tests/run-all.sh:3), invoking each sequentially with `bash`, so the FIRST failing suite aborts the entire run - and the epic-189-a1 suites sit at tests/run-all.sh:57-67, positions 49 through 59 of the 60, behind 48 unrelated suites. MEASURED THIS ROUND rather than assumed or inherited: a full `bash tests/run-all.sh` against an isolated `git clone --local` of HEAD (8f853228) in a throwaway scratch directory started 21 suites and aborted at the 21st, tests/turn-first-workflow.tests.sh - `not ok: implementation report template omits: ## Output Paths And Hashes`, exit 1 - so the aggregate runner never reaches the epic-189 suites at all. That assertion reads $IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT_TEMPLATE, resolved at tests/turn-first-workflow.tests.sh:8 to plugins/sdd-implementation/templates/implementation-report.template.md and asserted at :290; T-011 does not touch that file. `git diff --name-only 9652430e HEAD` lists 21 paths (9652430e = `git rev-parse --short 3dd2567d^`, the commit immediately before T-011's first commit), and the only three under plugins/ are the three unprotected consumer SKILL.md files this task revises. The abort is therefore NOT attributable to T-011. NOTE ON A STALE CLAIM, deliberately not repeated: the T-006..T-009 regression logs named tests/prepare-panelist.tests.sh as run-all's abort point. That was disproven by measurement during T-010's round (the suite passes 32/0, exit 0) and is recorded as a correction in reports/notes/epic-189-a1-carryover-items.md. The exclusion still holds; only the abort point has moved, and the abort point stated above is this round's own measurement. Set is the epic-189-a1 suites OTHER than T-011's own (which is recorded in focused-tests.log): TEN suites, TWENTY runs, now including hook-guard-epic-a1-boundary - T-010's own focused suite, which T-010's chain therefore excluded from its regression set and which has since landed. Every sh-lane run below is invoked with `bash`, not POSIX `sh`, matching the T-007..T-010 regression logs: suites across this epic's guard surface use process substitution and abort under POSIX `sh`. OBSERVED TALLY CHANGE, recorded rather than glossed: project-context-schema now reports 44/0 in both lanes where T-010's regression log recorded 41/0. The three added assertions come from commit ad7ed305 (T-001's seq0367 quality-gate remedy), which landed after T-010's chain and before T-011's first commit - `git log --oneline a8913080..HEAD -- tests/project-context-schema.tests.sh tests/project-context-schema.tests.ps1` names that commit and no other. Not a T-011 change. All twenty runs below exit 0. ===
