=== SUPPLEMENTARY (BEYOND the required T-011 regression set) ===
T-011 revises documented contracts and unprotected consumer prose; it does not
touch the live guard, so these three adjacent guard suites are not its blast
radius in the way they were T-010's. They are recorded here for continuity
with the T-009 and T-010 Done chains, which both recorded the same three, and
because the two failures below must be re-stated as pre-existing rather than
quietly dropped. Their result does NOT gate the `regression` check, whose
evidence is the twenty green runs above.

TWO failures appear in this section. Both are PRE-EXISTING and neither is
attributable to T-011. Each is PROVEN pre-existing here by this round's own
re-measurement rather than by citing the carryover note. Shared basis:

  $ git rev-parse --short 3dd2567d^
  9652430e            # the commit immediately BEFORE T-011's first commit
  $ git log --oneline 9652430e..HEAD -- tests/guards.tests.sh \
      tests/phase2-guard-invariants.tests.ps1 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/
  (no output - 0 commits; T-011's entire range touches neither suite nor any
   guard script, and `git diff --stat 9652430e HEAD -- \
   plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/` is empty)

DISCLOSURE 1 - tests/phase2-guard-invariants.tests.ps1 FAILS here
(59 passed, 9 failed, exit 1). Reproduced against the pre-T-011 tree:

  $ git archive 9652430e | tar -x -C <scratch dir>
  $ cd <scratch dir> && pwsh -NoProfile -File tests/phase2-guard-invariants.tests.ps1
  phase2-guard-invariants.tests.ps1: 59 passed, 9 failed   (exit 1)
  $ diff <pre-T-011 FAIL lines> <current-HEAD FAIL lines>
  (no output - identical 9-line failure set, sha256
   5f1ffc4f78d5873a9f6c50364a6a2bf85f7f134c9050eb08312137c79fbf78bc both sides)

All nine are TEST-013 install/rollback cases that depend on Windows/NTFS
semantics (junctions, held handles, out-of-inventory hard-link aliases, the
fixed native replacement API) being exercised on macOS; the bash twin of the
same suite passes 33/0 here.

DISCLOSURE 2 - tests/guards.tests.sh is INVOCATION-DEPENDENT here:

  $ bash tests/guards.tests.sh
  Results: 133 passed, 0 failed.         (exit 0)
  $ sh tests/guards.tests.sh
  FAIL: sh: copilot deny -> JSON deny ...
  (46 ok lines, no "Results:" line, exit 2 - the run aborts)

The failing case name labels the guard's `sh` IMPLEMENTATION, not the harness
shell: this suite labels every case sh:/py:/node: by which guard runtime it
drives. The deny JSON that case emits carries an embedded newline, which the
POSIX-sh harness path does not survive. Reproduced against the pre-T-011 tree:

  $ git archive 9652430e | tar -x -C <scratch dir>
  $ cd <scratch dir> && sh tests/guards.tests.sh
  FAIL: sh: copilot deny -> JSON deny ...   (exit 2)
  $ diff <pre-T-011 sh-lane output> <current-HEAD sh-lane output>
  (no output - byte-identical, 48 lines each; sha256
   0bdd7b370d972aff62a442ba6335c09e11a74d32e8cf64217f77c7ccf5616afb both sides)

That digest is the SAME value T-010's regression log recorded for this lane,
so the failure is byte-for-byte unchanged across both tasks' rounds.

CARRYOVER STATUS, checked on disk this round rather than repeated from the
prior log: BOTH failures are now written up in
reports/notes/epic-189-a1-carryover-items.md - disclosure 1 under the section
"既存不具合: phase2-guard-invariants の pwsh レーンが macOS で 9 件失敗"
(recorded during T-009's Done chain) and disclosure 2 under "既存不具合:
guards スイートが POSIX `sh` 起動時のみ 1 件失敗" (added by commit 757dd104,
after T-010's chain flagged it as the one still missing). T-010's log's "NOT
yet written up" note is therefore discharged; nothing new is owed here.

